            "creation_time": "2021-01-04T15:09:49Z",
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "bug_id": 18025,
            "text": "Sample package:\n\n```\ndir <- file.path(tempdir(), \"testPkg\")\ndir.create(file.path(dir, \"R\"), recursive = TRUE)\nwriteLines(\"Package: testPkg\\nVersion: 0.0.1\", file.path(dir, \"DESCRIPTION\"))\nwriteLines(\"foo = function() base::message('hi')\", file.path(dir, \"R\", \"foo.R\"))\nwriteLines(\"export(foo)\", file.path(dir, \"NAMESPACE\"))\n```\n\nAnd try to extract messages:\n\n```\ntools::xgettext(dir)\n# list()\n```\n\nc.f. if `base::` is removed:\n\n```\n# $`/tmp/RtmpR0ZIwk/testPkg/R/foo.R`\n# hi\n```\n\nI see ~200 such uses on CRAN, e.g. for stop:\n\nhttps://github.com/search?l=R&q=%22base%3A%3Astop%22+org%3Acran&type=Code\n\nSo it's not the most crucial thing in the world, however, IINM, the fix is not particularly involved.",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "id": 96971,
            "time": "2021-01-04T15:09:49Z",
            "is_private": false
          },
          {
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": 2790,
            "time": "2021-01-04T16:17:57Z",
            "id": 96972,
            "is_private": false,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "creation_time": "2021-01-04T16:17:57Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 2790\nExtend xgettext/xngettext to include namespace-qualified calls\n\nAn implementation is here.\n\nAdded new helper functions to src/library/tools/R/utils.R which greatly simplify things. Happy to reorganize but I think the basic idea of the patch is pretty straightforward -- instead of only looking for plain calls (`is.name(e) && as.character(e) %in% list_of_calls`), we also check if it's a qualified namespace call from base to `list_of_calls`, which means `is.call(e)` and `e[[1]]` is `::`, `e[[2]]` is `base`, and `e[[3]] %in% list_of_calls`.\n\nConfirmed this works locally & didn't notice any issues from `make check`.",
            "bug_id": 18025,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 1
          }
        ]
      }
